  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, I'm not quite sure how instance creation is handled for portals placed via VRC Portal Markers; however, it seems that players consistently get split into different instances as-is. This is especially prevalent when arriving at private worlds.\n\nPerhaps there's a better solution than this, but I propose that, if possible, destination instances should be reserved upon creation of the origin instance. Or at least have the option in the SDK to do so.\n\nPresumably, this could go hand-in-hand with similar customization of what occurs with the destination instance. Such as limiting player count, setting public/friends/invite, and setting arrival spawn point.\n\n\nRelated suggestions:\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/add-ability-specifying-world-instance-and-accessibility-to-vrcportalmarker\n\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/give-portals-the-ability-to-set-a-destination-spawn-location",
